* Goroutines

A ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000001⟫⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000002⟫⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000003⟫ is a lightweight thread managed by the Go runtime.

⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000004⟫

starts a new ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000005⟫ running

⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000006⟫

The evaluation of ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000007⟫f⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000008⟫, ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000009⟫x⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000010⟫, ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000011⟫y⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000012⟫, and ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000013⟫z⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000014⟫ happens in the current ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000015⟫ and the execution of ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000016⟫f⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000017⟫ happens in the new ⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000018⟫.

Goroutines run in the same address space, so access to shared memory must be synchronized. The [[⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000019⟫][⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000020⟫sync⟪GTI18N_d0a9c450_000021⟫]] package provides useful primitives, although you won't need them much in Go as there are other primitives. (See the next slide.)

